# Outputs are regenerated by the scripts and are not committed, except for the files
# the paper and the README read: the three-window table, the CRSP rebuild comparisons
# (the only way a reader without a WRDS subscription can see them) and the forecasting
# results of the anomaly panel and of Stage 1 (so the paper renders without refitting).
# Every Stage 1 file is an aggregate: no stock-month row leaves the machine that holds
# the WRDS data.
output/*
!output/fig02_decay.png
!output/result1_summary.txt
!output/result1_windows.csv
!output/fig04_rebuild.png
!output/rebuild_summary.txt
!output/rebuild_Size.csv
!output/rebuild_Mom12m.csv
!output/fig05_r2.png
!output/fig05_decay.png
!output/fig05_portfolio.png
!output/ml_summary.txt
!output/ml_r2.csv
!output/ml_dm.csv
!output/ml_portfolio.csv
!output/ml_importance.csv
!output/ml_decay_curve.csv
!output/ml_tuning.csv
!output/ml_r2_sensitivity.csv
!output/ml_counts.csv
!output/stage1_run.json
!output/stage1_r2.csv
!output/stage1_ic.csv
!output/stage1_dm.csv
!output/stage1_portfolio_summary.csv
!output/stage1_portfolios_monthly.csv
!output/stage1_spreads_panel.csv
!output/stage1_spreads_traded.csv
!output/stage1_target.csv
!output/stage1_target_top.csv
!output/stage1_tuning.csv
!output/stage1_timing.csv
!output/stage1_importance.csv
!output/stage1_huber_coef.csv
!output/stage1_char_ic.csv
!output/stage1_eventtime.csv
!output/fig07_eventtime.png
!output/fig07_decomposition.png
!output/fig07_r2_by_year.png

# Script backups
*.bak_*

# Quarto build products. The .qmd is the source; the intermediate render and the
# generated notebook are not committed.
paper/_output/
paper/_freeze/
paper/.quarto/
paper/*.ipynb
.quarto/

# docs/ is NOT ignored. It holds the single self-contained HTML that GitHub Pages
# serves, produced by paper/publish.sh. Committing a build artefact is deliberate
# here: the render needs the Chen-Zimmermann files, which are not redistributable
# and so are not in the repo, which means no CI job could rebuild the page.

# A private working file: six method questions to answer in writing. The answers now
# live in paper/alpha-decay.qmd, where they are argued rather than listed, so the
# worksheet itself is not part of the published project.
DECISIONS.md

# Two working files that are not part of this project. PROFILE_README.md is a draft of
# a GitHub profile page and belongs in the profile repository; GIT_GUIDE.md is a git
# tutorial written while setting this up. Neither is about alpha decay.
PROFILE_README.md
GIT_GUIDE.md
